api.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every operation, method, path, parameter, schema, status code, and security rule in the OpenAPI contract; expose no undocumented operations or feedlot product screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined authentication, session, dashboard, and filtered lot data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Support procurement-record preview and import, and persist PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen allocation traceability, including matching and conflict results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined forecasts, forecast settings, metrics, insights, planner actions, and weight histories, and persist valid setting and action updates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined inventory, movements, projections, and exports, and persist valid inventory changes in PostgreSQL.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined rations and optimization and approval results, and persist valid ration changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Return and persist contract-defined feed-plan details, calculated quantities, audit state, reviews, and execution status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Persist feeding events, corrections, and voids, and return contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and updated lot feed totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined, permission-filtered operational, feed-to-gain, and profitability reports, calculations, summaries, and requested exports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Support sample-data status and loading without duplicates, and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Store contract domain data in PostgreSQL using the configured App connection and preserve successful writes across API process restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, use SeedData.Run at startup to add 3 to 5 believable, contract-example-derived sample rows to each empty application table, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing seed-write errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false and collections are empty, serve collection operations with empty lists; tests must create their own records when nonempty data is required.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}